{
  "id": "36-in-state-lost",
  "title": "The daemon's input state is not the one the client talked to: rotate `ie`, never resend",
  "spec": "5.4",
  "description": "WELCOME.inGen identifies the daemon's input.log generation (new when the state is created from scratch). A changed inGen, or inHi below what the client already had acknowledged (an older copy of the state, e.g. the cloned CT of 2026-10-31), makes the client rotate `ie` for that link: counters restart at 1, acknowledged input is never resent, unacknowledged input is shown 'unknown'. Otherwise the next iseq is max(local, inHi) + 1 and the outbox above inHi is resent in order.",
  "framing": "every frame: u32be len | u8 type | u8 flags | u16be hlen | header JSON | blob; each (conn, dir) stream starts with the 8-byte magic",
